{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context (discovered during RP-05 S2d; closes an RP-05 residual gap)\nThe py3.13 help-rendering divergences RP-05 S2d fixed — argparse (1) rendering an option with BOTH short+long forms as `-o, --output X` (metavar once) vs pre-3.13 `-o X, --output X`, and (2) keeping a subparsers `{choices} ...` usage line unwrapped where pre-3.13 wrapped the `...` — are pinned to a single deterministic rendering ONLY inside `RebarHelpFormatter` (src/rebar/_cli/_parser.py: the `_format_action_invocation` and `_format_usage` overrides, plus a FIXED width of 80).\n\nOf the advanced parser factories (src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/), only `bridge` was switched to `RebarHelpFormatter`; the rest — metrics, config, audit, llm_eval, enrich, certs, bridge_arms, llm, jira, workflow, reconcile, identity — still explicitly pass `formatter_class=argparse.HelpFormatter`, overriding `build_argument_parser`'s `RebarHelpFormatter` default back to stock (22 call sites).\n\n## Problem (two concrete defects, not merely latent)\n1. **Width inconsistency in committed artifacts.** `RebarHelpFormatter` wraps help at width 80; stock `argparse.HelpFormatter` wraps at 78 (argparse subtracts 2 from the terminal width only in its `width=None` branch). So committed artifacts are already inconsistent: `bridge.txt` (RebarHelpFormatter) is width-80 while `bridge-fsck.txt` (stock, via bridge_arms) is width-78.\n2. **py3.13 staleness trap.** Any stock-formatter advanced parser whose help gains a short+long metavar option, or whose usage line wraps, would render differently on py3.13 than 3.11/3.12 — silently making `scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check` (and the docs reference `--check`) STALE on the py3.13 CI cell only: exactly the failure S2d spent multiple patchsets chasing.\n\n## Fix\nSwitch every remaining advanced parser factory from `argparse.HelpFormatter` to the version-pinned `RebarHelpFormatter` (import it from `rebar._cli._parser`; the simplest edit is to drop the explicit override so `build_argument_parser` applies its `RebarHelpFormatter` default, or pass it explicitly). Regenerate the derived help + docs artifacts: exactly one wrapping artifact changes — `bridge-fsck.txt` moves from width-78 to the canonical width-80 form (a deliberate, reviewed regeneration; other artifacts are byte-unchanged). Add a contract test that FAILS if any registered parser factory renders through a non-`RebarHelpFormatter` formatter, so the trap cannot be reintroduced.\n\n## Compatibility / Rollback\nNo runtime handler, event, ticket, or persisted-data change. Rollback restores the prior formatter override. Only generated help/doc artifacts and one committed help file change.\n\n## Testing\n- Contract test: iterate the route registry, resolve each `parser_factory`, assert `type(parser.formatter_class) is/subclasses RebarHelpFormatter` (or the parser's `_get_formatter()` is a RebarHelpFormatter) — RED before the switch for the 12 stock files, GREEN after.\n- Regenerate + `gen_cli_help.py --check` and `gen_cli_reference.py --check` both rc=0.\n- Byte-identical determinism verified across py3.11 / 3.12 / 3.13.15 (the whole point: all advanced artifacts now version-stable).\n- Existing help-serving / overview-coverage / facade suites stay green with the regenerated `bridge-fsck.txt`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every core and advanced parser factory renders help through the version-pinned `RebarHelpFormatter`; no factory passes `formatter_class=argparse.HelpFormatter`.\n- [ ] A contract test fails if any registered factory uses a non-pinned formatter (RED before the switch, GREEN after).\n- [ ] `gen_cli_help.py --check` and `gen_cli_reference.py --check` are rc=0 and byte-identical across py3.11 / 3.12 / 3.13.15.\n- [ ] The only committed help-artifact byte change is `bridge-fsck.txt` regenerated to the canonical width-80 form; all other artifacts are byte-unchanged, and help-serving/overview/facade suites stay green."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787327687962209001,"uuid":"7743c3ab-d499-405a-9f04-cb24da1828d2"}